<description>
Crop out the grid half containing the two aligned marker pixels, then erase the markers to background.

Input structure
- The grid has a dominant background color and one non-background marker color
  that appears as exactly two cells.
- The marker cells are aligned either in one row or one column and both lie
  in the same half along that direction.
- Other non-background pixels are content inside one or both halves.

Rule
- If the markers share a row, keep the left or right half whose columns
  contain them.
- If the markers share a column, keep the top or bottom half whose rows
  contain them.
- In the kept half, recolor the marker pixels to the background color.

Key insight
- The two marker pixels are not part of the picture; their alignment and
  half-position identify which half of the doubled canvas is the answer.
</description>
<annotation>
{
  "type": "transform_in_place",
  "src": "half-grid region containing the two aligned marker pixels",
  "transform": "crop to that half; use row-aligned markers to choose left/right and column-aligned markers to choose top/bottom, then recolor marker pixels to bg",
  "grid_shape": "same height and half width for row-aligned markers; half height and same width for column-aligned markers"
}
</annotation>
<generation_spec>
```yaml
spec:
  grid: 4-20 rows x 8-30 cols, both dimensions even
  background: 8 (azure), dominant
  colors: exactly 2 non-bg colors — 1 content color + gray(5) as marker
  marker:
    color: 5 (gray), exactly 2 pixels
    alignment: both in same row OR same column, gap of exactly 2 between them
    placement: on a grid boundary edge (row 0, row H-1, col 0, or col W-1)
    half: both pixels lie entirely within one half along their aligned axis
    axis: if same-row -> horizontal split (left/right); if same-col -> vertical split (top/bottom)
  content:
    color: any non-bg non-marker color (1-4,7,9 observed)
    pattern: sparse dot pattern — pixels at every-other-column positions within content rows, col gap=2
    content rows have varying row gaps (1-3); not all rows carry content
    spans both halves of the grid (content exists in kept and discarded halves)
    content pixels never overlap marker pixel positions [observed]
    density: 8-25% of output half cells
  split_rule: the grid dimension along the marker alignment axis is even; halve along that axis
  output: the half containing the marker pixels, with marker pixels replaced by bg

generation_strategy:
  approach: output-first
  steps:
    1. Pick split axis (row or col) and output half dimensions (H_half x W or H x W_half), both even, total grid 4-20 rows x 8-30 cols
